    <svg width="0" height="0" style="position:absolute" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <symbol id="i-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="i-down-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 5l13 13M18 8v10H8" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="i-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M7.6 12.4l3 3 5.8-6.2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
          <symbol id="i-up-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 18L18 6M8 6h10v10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></symbol>
    </svg>

    <section class="hero hero-about hero-services hero-legal hero-case" aria-labelledby="case-title">
      <span class="hbar hbar-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-3" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hbar hbar-4" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <div class="ah-copy">
        <p class="ah-label" data-reveal>Case study</p>
        <h1 id="case-title" data-speakable>
          <span class="line">Clothing</span><span class="line">E-commerce</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="ah-intro" data-reveal data-speakable>An online storefront concept for a fashion brand</p>
      </div>

      <div class="svc-index cs-meta" role="group" aria-label="Project details">
        <ol>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Type</span><span class="si-t">E-commerce Website Concept</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Industry</span><span class="si-t">Fashion / Retail</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Role</span><span class="si-t">Website Design &amp; Front-End Development</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Platform</span><span class="si-t">Systeme.io</span></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><div class="si-row"><span class="si-n">Development</span><span class="si-t">Custom HTML, CSS &amp; JavaScript</span></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark pj cs-open" id="overview" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>Overview</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="overview-title">Building an online storefront around the products and the brand.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>A clothing website needs to do more than display products. It needs to communicate the brand’s identity, present its collection clearly, and make it easy for visitors to explore what is available.</p><p data-rise>This e-commerce concept explores how a fashion brand can bring its visual identity and product presentation together through a structured online storefront.</p>
            <div class="pj-actions" data-rise><a class="cta cta-menu" href="https://madfunneldesignecommerce.systeme.io/clothingdemo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>View Live Concept</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-up-right"/></svg></a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figure class="pj-shot cs-shot" style="--ar:16 / 9"><a class="pj-link" href="https://madfunneldesignecommerce.systeme.io/clothingdemo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="assets/img/project-clothing.webp" alt="Clothing e-commerce website concept: the homepage headline reads Fade Into Black, over a photo of two people in streetwear on a city rooftop, with a Shop the Drop button." width="1280" height="720" decoding="async"><span class="pj-hint" aria-hidden="true">View live</span></a><figcaption>Homepage screenshot of the live concept</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-white cs-sec" id="challenge" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Design Challenge</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="challenge-title">Balancing brand identity with a practical shopping experience.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>Fashion is highly visual, but an online store still needs a clear structure. Visitors should be able to explore products, understand what is being offered, and move through the shopping experience without unnecessary friction.</p><p data-rise>The design direction focused on three priorities:</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-points"><li data-rise><h3>Brand presentation</h3><p>establish a recognizable visual identity that gives the storefront its own character.</p></li><li data-rise><h3>Product visibility</h3><p>make product imagery and essential product information easy to explore.</p></li><li data-rise><h3>Shopping navigation</h3><p>create a clear path between browsing the collection and taking the next step.</p></li></ul>
        <div class="cs-after"><p data-rise>The goal was to make the storefront feel like a cohesive fashion brand rather than a generic product catalog.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-amber cs-sec" id="direction" aria-labelledby="direction-title">
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Visual Direction</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="direction-title">Letting the brand and collection define the experience.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The design uses an editorial approach to bring together product imagery, typography, and layout.</p><p data-rise>Instead of treating the storefront as a collection of identical product blocks, the visual direction aims to give the brand a consistent identity while keeping product discovery straightforward.</p><p data-rise>Key design considerations included:</p>
            <ul class="cs-list" data-rise><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>A distinct opening section that introduces the fashion brand.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Product-focused layouts that give collection imagery room to stand out.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Typography and spacing that reinforce the brand’s personality.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Consistent styling across the storefront.</span></li><li><svg width="22" height="22" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Clear navigation between the main shopping sections.</span></li></ul>
            <p data-rise>The visual system was designed to support product discovery without distracting from the products themselves.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark cs-sec" id="development" aria-labelledby="development-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Development</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="development-title">Bringing the storefront together through custom front-end work.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The concept was developed using Systeme.io, with custom code used to refine the storefront’s visual presentation and layout.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="dm-rows cs-tools"><li><h3 data-rise>Systeme.io</h3><div data-rise><p>Used as the website platform and publishing environment.</p></div></li><li><h3 data-rise>Custom HTML &amp; CSS</h3><div data-rise><p>Used to build and refine the storefront layout, product presentation, and responsive styling.</p></div></li><li><h3 data-rise>JavaScript</h3><div data-rise><p>Used for custom interface behavior where required.</p></div></li></ul>
        <div class="cs-after"><p data-rise>The approach allowed the storefront to have a more tailored presentation than a standard page-builder layout.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-white cs-sec" id="build" aria-labelledby="build-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>What Went Into the Build</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="build-title">Design decisions translated into a working website concept.</h2>
          </header>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-table" data-rise><table><caption class="sr-only">Clothing E-commerce: what went into the build</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Area</th><th scope="col">Implementation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Visual direction</th><td>Fashion-focused brand presentation</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Storefront layout</th><td>Product and collection presentation</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">User experience</th><td>Shopping-oriented navigation</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Typography</th><td>Brand-aligned visual hierarchy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Front-end</th><td>Custom HTML, CSS and JavaScript</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Platform</th><td>Systeme.io</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Responsive design</th><td>Adapted layouts for desktop and mobile</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-dark cs-sec" id="result" aria-labelledby="result-title">
      <div class="ab-in">
        <div class="ab-split">
          <header class="ab-head">
            <p class="ab-k" data-rise>The Result</p>
            <h2 class="cs-h2" id="result-title">A storefront concept that connects brand presentation and product discovery.</h2>
          </header>
          <div class="ab-body">
            <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>The Clothing E-commerce concept demonstrates how a fashion brand can present its identity and collection through a cohesive online storefront.</p><p data-rise>It brings together visual direction, product-focused layouts, and custom front-end development to create an experience centered on browsing and exploring a collection.</p><p data-rise>It reflects my approach to e-commerce design: the storefront should represent the brand while making the products easy to discover.</p>
            <p class="cs-note" data-rise><em>This is an independent e-commerce website concept, not a commissioned client store. It does not represent verified sales, transactions, or business performance.</em></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <nav class="cs-next" aria-label="More case studies" data-rise>
          <a href="/projects#clothing-ecommerce"><span class="cs-next-k">All projects</span><span class="cs-next-t">Back to the project overview</span></a>
          <a href="/case-black-chauffeur"><span class="cs-next-k">Next case study</span><span class="cs-next-t">Black Chauffeur</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab ab-amber ab-cta" id="lets-talk" aria-labelledby="talk-title">
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-l" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="ab-bar ab-bar-r" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="ab-in">
        <h2 class="cs-cta-h" id="talk-title">Planning an Online Store?</h2>
        <div class="ab-cta-body">
          <p class="ab-lead" data-rise>Your storefront is often where customers first experience your brand. It should make your products easy to explore while giving people a clear understanding of what makes your business different.</p>
          <p data-rise>I design and develop e-commerce websites that bring product presentation, brand identity, and shopping navigation together.</p>
          <div class="ab-cta-actions" data-rise>
            <a class="cta cta-solid" href="https://calendly.com/-aldrichmatthew/15mins"><span>Book a Free Strategy Call</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
            <a class="cta cta-ghost" href="/projects"><span>Explore More Projects</span><svg width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  
</Base>
